# (b) You come back before 20 minutes: the new message cancels the countdown; the next reply's end starts a new one.
title:   Coming back early cancels the timer
caption: You send a new message after nine minutes. That cancels the countdown, so nothing is compacted while you are working. When Claude finishes that reply, a fresh 20-minute countdown starts.
note:    1 column = 1 minute; the ≈ break skips ten quiet minutes. Every finished reply starts the countdown again from zero; there is never more than one.
break:   +10 min

time           0    5m   10m  15m  ≈ 30m
claude      -S~E--------S~~~E------≈-----
countdown      [========x   [======≈====>
compaction  -----------------------≈-----

legend
S  message sent — you ask, Claude starts  blue
~  Claude working  teal
E  reply done — the countdown starts  teal
=  idle countdown · 20 min  violet
x  cancelled — by your new message  coral
